# Markdown Integration Test

Tests altodo format embedded in Markdown content.


## Introduction

This is a regular Markdown paragraph. It can contain **bold text**, *italic text*, 
and `inline code`. altodo tasks can be embedded anywhere in the document.

[ ] This is an altodo task in the middle of Markdown content


## Code Blocks

Markdown code blocks should not be interpreted as altodo:

```
[ ] This is NOT an altodo task (it's in a code block)
/// This is NOT a comment (it's in a code block)
    #tag is just text here
```

But outside the code block:

[x] This IS an altodo task #real-tag


## Inline Code

Inline code should not be interpreted: `[ ] not a task` and `#not-a-tag`.

But this is real: [ ] Real task with #real-tag


## Lists

Regular Markdown lists:

- Item 1
- Item 2
  - Nested item

altodo tasks:

[ ] Task 1
[ ] 
[ ] Task 2
    [ ] Nested task


## Links and Images

Regular Markdown link: [Example](https://example.com)

[ ] Task with link: Check [documentation](https://docs.example.com) #work


## Blockquotes

> This is a blockquote.
> It can contain multiple lines.

[ ] Task after blockquote


## Tables

| Column 1 | Column 2 |
|----------|----------|
| Data 1   | Data 2   |

[ ] Task after table


## Horizontal Rules

-----

[ ] Task after horizontal rule

-----


## Mixed Content

Here's a paragraph with **bold** and *italic* text.

[ ] + Important task #urgent
    Task details in multi-line comment.
    More details here.
    /// This task needs immediate attention

Another paragraph with `inline code` and a [link](https://example.com).

[ ] Task with inline markup __bold__ _italic_ **bold** *italic* `code`
[@] In-progress task 2026-02-15 -> 2026-02-20 @john
    [ ] Subtask 1
    [ ] Subtask 2

Final paragraph.


## Indented Tasks Are Never Markdown Code Blocks

In Markdown, a line indented by 4 spaces after a blank line is a code block. altodo uses
indentation for nesting, so the indented task lines below are tasks (check the faces and
that C-c C-x toggles them).

[ ] Parent task

    [ ] Child task after a blank line
    
        [ ] Grandchild task after a space-only line


## Fenced Code Blocks Inside Comments

[ ] Task with a code sample
    Run this:
    ```elisp
    (altodo-mode)
    [ ] this line is text inside the code block
    ```
    After the block, the comment continues.
